  intro: [
    'Murchison Falls National Park is Uganda\'s largest national park at 3,840 km², stretching from the edge of the Albertine Rift Valley in the west to the vast savannah plains of the north bank. The park takes its name from the most dramatic feature on the entire length of the Nile — the point where the world\'s longest river is forced through a gap just 7 metres wide before plunging 43 metres into the gorge below in a thundering cascade of white water.',
