      'The afternoon boat safari from Paraa to the base of Murchison Falls is one of the most celebrated wildlife experiences in all of Uganda. The 3-hour journey along the Victoria Nile passes enormous pods of hippos, 5-metre Nile crocodiles basking on every bank, elephants drinking at the water\'s edge and an extraordinary variety of waterbirds including the rare shoebill stork on the river delta.',
      'The boat approaches within metres of the falls at the end of the run — the spray and the roar of the water at close range are genuinely overwhelming. Return is by the same route. Evening departures offer the best light for photography.',
