      'The north bank of the Nile inside Murchison Falls is one of the finest game drive destinations in East Africa. The open savannah supports large herds of Uganda kobs, Rothschild\'s giraffes (one of the world\'s most endangered giraffe subspecies), Jackson\'s hartebeests, oribi and buffaloes. Lions are regularly seen on and around the Buligi Game Tracks.',
      'Morning game drives at first light are the most productive for predators. Late afternoon drives catch the golden hour light on the giraffes and the large kob herds returning to the river. The south bank has denser vegetation and is particularly good for primates and forest birds.',
